---
description: Block runtime beyond the current stage and unbounded AI data access
alwaysApply: false
---

Apply when adding Python packages, integrations, SQL, LLM calls, or agents.

Not allowed until its stage (and, where it adds a dependency or top-level package, an ADR) lands:

- Metrics, detection, cohort, Jev, policy, incident, investigation, API or UI code
- LLM clients and prompt pipelines that ingest events
- Tools that execute arbitrary SQL or mutate payments
- Vector DB / RAG
- Autonomous refund/retry/remediation

Allowed today: the simulator and the ClickHouse loader (`src/anomalyos/simulation`, ADR-020).
Approved analytical access, when it exists, must be typed interfaces (`INV-003`), never model-authored SQL (`INV-002`).
